<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 7 June, from 879 to 1942.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/879">879 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John VIII recognises Croatia under Duke Branimir</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope John VIII recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> as an independent state and Branimir as its duke. Branimir had come to power by overthrowing Duke Zdeslav, a Byzantine client, and his reign turned Croatia firmly towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-croatia">Duchy of Croatia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/branimir-of-croatia">Branimir of Croatia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1002">1002 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,024 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry II is elected and crowned King of Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-bavaria">Henry II, Duke of Bavaria</a> and second cousin of Emperor Otto III, was elected and crowned King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> after Otto's sudden death. The last Ottonian ruler, he was crowned emperor by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-benedict-viii">Pope Benedict VIII</a> in 1014.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Otto III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1099">1099 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">927 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Crusade begins the siege of Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The crusader armies reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and invested the city. They stormed it on 15 July and massacred many of its Muslim and Jewish inhabitants.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1420">1420 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">606 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Venice captures Udine, ending the independence of the Patria del Friuli</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Venetian troops took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udine">Udine</a> after a long siege, and Gemona, San Daniele, Venzone and Tolmezzo soon followed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> annexed the Patria del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>, ending the temporal rule of the Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udine">Udine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1494">1494 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">532 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spain and Portugal sign the Treaty of Tordesillas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The two kingdoms divided newly found lands along a meridian 370 leagues west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-verde">Cape Verde</a>. The line later gave Portugal its claim to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tordesillas">Treaty of Tordesillas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-verde">Cape Verde</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1692">1692 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">334 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake sinks much of Port Royal, Jamaica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A violent earthquake plunged two-thirds of the buccaneer town into the sea, killing some 2,000 people at once. Many saw it as divine judgement on 'the wickedest city on Earth'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard Henry Lee moves for American independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lee proposed that 'these United Colonies are, and of right ought to be, free and independent States'. Congress adopted the resolution on 2 July.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Norway dissolves its union with Sweden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Norwegian parliament declared that King Oscar II had ceased to rule as King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> accepted the separation peacefully after a referendum, and Norway chose a Danish prince as king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Midway ends with the sinking of Yorktown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The damaged carrier USS Yorktown finally sank as the battle closed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s loss of four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aircraft-carrier">fleet carriers</a> ended its naval superiority in the Pacific.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Battle of Midway</a></div></div></li></ol>
